Title:
Mole — Binary Ninja plugin for backward slicing–driven static taint analysis

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Mole is a Binary Ninja plugin that finds “interesting” data-flow paths in binaries by performing backward slicing on MLIL (SSA) variables and using that as the basis for static taint analysis.  
- It targets the common reverse-engineering problem of quickly identifying where untrusted inputs (sources) can influence sensitive operations (sinks), helping prioritize potential vulnerability candidates.  
- Users define sources/sinks via UI or config files, then Mole enumerates and visualizes paths, prints instructions/call sequences, and supports grouping similar paths (e.g., by source/sink or call sequence).  
- It supports inter-procedural slicing (approximate caller resolution) and basic pointer tracking with known limitations (e.g., globals not fully tracked).  
- Results can be persisted into the Binary Ninja `.bndb` database or exported/imported for headless batch analysis across many binaries.  
- An optional AI mode integrates with LLMs via the OpenAI API to triage paths (vuln classification/severity) and request additional binary context.  
- Useful primarily for vulnerability researchers, reverse engineers, and red team/pentest operators doing binary auditing; also relevant to defenders doing firmware/software assurance.  
- Notable example: demonstrated use in surfacing CVE-2021-4045 (TP-Link Tapo C200 command injection).

Technical Focus:
- Binary Ninja MLIL (SSA) analysis
- Backward program slicing (data-flow slicing)
- Static taint analysis (source-to-sink path discovery)
- Inter-procedural analysis across function boundaries
- Pointer/value tracking approximations
- Headless automation + path persistence/export; optional LLM-assisted triage (OpenAI API)

Use Cases:
- Firmware/binary vulnerability discovery by tracing untrusted input to dangerous sinks
- Rapid triage and prioritization of candidate exploit paths in large codebases
- Batch headless scanning of many binaries and later interactive review in Binary Ninja
- Comparing and grouping similar data-flow paths to reduce analyst workload
- Assisted reporting/triage using LLM-based path classification (optional)

Keywords:
Binary Ninja, MLIL, SSA, backward slicing, program slicing, static taint analysis, interprocedural analysis, pointer analysis, data-flow, source-to-sink, vulnerability research, reverse engineering, headless analysis, .bndb, path grouping, call graph, CVE-2021-4045, command injection, OpenAI API, LLM triage